WEBVTT

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.216
Hmm.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.844
Um... Ah, nah.

00:00:10.928 --> 00:00:12.513
Mm... Ah.

00:00:12.638 --> 00:00:14.097
Yeah.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:19.019
Goin' through the 'bot wash

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:22.731
Goin' through the robot wash

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:25.275
Come on, y'all
And sing it with me

00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:26.652
'Bot wash

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:29.279
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa

00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:30.697
'Bot wash, yeah

00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:35.327
Hmm!

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:40.040
Oh...

00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:47.297
Ah.

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:53.512
Oh!

00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:28.881
Hey, I'm Elzar.

00:01:28.964 --> 00:01:30.299
Welcome to the show.

00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:33.343
You know, you don't have
to drive all the way to Neptune

00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:35.387
for great Neptunian food.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.639
Today, we're gonna kick it up a notch

00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:41.518
as I show you how to fricassee
a mouthwatering Neptunian slug.

00:01:41.602 --> 00:01:43.020
Whoo-whee!

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:47.232
Now, while you're greasing the pan
and preheating your oven to 3,500 degrees,

00:01:47.316 --> 00:01:50.611
you're gonna separate the yolk
from your genetically enhanced eggplant,

00:01:50.694 --> 00:01:53.864
and then give the whole thing a good blast
from your spice weasel.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:54.948
Bam!

00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:56.200
Hey, what you watching?

00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:57.367
Uh, nothing.

00:01:57.451 --> 00:01:58.785
Is that a cooking show?

00:01:58.869 --> 00:02:00.913
No, of course not.

00:02:00.996 --> 00:02:03.123
It was, uh...

00:02:03.207 --> 00:02:04.875
Porno. Yeah, that's it.

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.628
Bender, I didn't know you liked cooking.

00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:09.129
That's so cute.

00:02:09.213 --> 00:02:11.131
Aw, it's true.

00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:13.383
I've been hiding it for so long.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:16.261
It's okay, Bender. I like cooking, too.

00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:17.513
Pansy.

00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:19.640
Of course, your most important ingredient

00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:22.851
Is this baby right here,
the Neptunian slug.

00:02:22.935 --> 00:02:26.104
You can get it in a can,
but to really do things right,

00:02:26.188 --> 00:02:28.565
you got to strangle yourself a fresh one.

00:02:30.776 --> 00:02:34.321
Now this is why you always want to use
cast iron cookware.

00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:45.582
Bender, mon,
it has come to my attention

00:02:45.666 --> 00:02:49.002
that this company has been paying you
to do nothing but loaf about on the couch.

00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:50.462
You call that a couch?

00:02:50.546 --> 00:02:52.089
I demand a pillow.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.716
I'm sorry, but if you want
to continue drawing a salary,

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.135
you've got to do more than watch
the cooking shows all day.

00:02:57.219 --> 00:02:59.263
Hmm...

00:02:59.763 --> 00:03:01.765
You're gonna be the ship's cook?

00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:04.643
Yeah. We're gonna kick it up a notch.
Bam!

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:07.604
I know you like cooking shows,
but you're a robot.

00:03:07.688 --> 00:03:09.356
You don't even have a sense of taste.

00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:13.986
Honey, I wouldn't talk about taste
if was wearing a lime green tank top.

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:15.070
Bam!

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:20.868
So this is little Neptune.

00:03:20.951 --> 00:03:26.123
Yep. Every chef knows this is the place
to get exotic gourmet ingredients.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.749
Among other things.

00:03:34.298 --> 00:03:35.799
Come on, man!

00:03:35.883 --> 00:03:38.594
Don't hold out on me like this!

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.346
Psst. You want to buy organ?

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.057
Fresh and cheap ready for transplant.

00:03:44.141 --> 00:03:47.102
- Ooh, what's this?
- Ah, it's X-ray eye.

00:03:47.186 --> 00:03:48.562
See through anything.

00:03:48.645 --> 00:03:51.148
Wait a minute. This says Z-ray.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.567
"Z" is just as good. In fact, it's better.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.152
It's two more than "X."

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:57.863
Hmm, I can see where
that would be an advantage.

00:03:57.946 --> 00:03:59.448
Do you take cash?

00:03:59.531 --> 00:04:01.366
Fry, you have to be more careful.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.744
You're not in the 20th century anymore.

00:04:03.827 --> 00:04:05.621
You don't know how things work here.

00:04:05.704 --> 00:04:07.164
I'm not a little kid, Leela.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.457
I grew up in this city.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.042
These are my people.

00:04:10.125 --> 00:04:11.585
- What up?
- Word.

00:04:11.668 --> 00:04:12.794
See?

00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:17.382
Wow! You guys sell
every kind of meat here except human.

00:04:17.466 --> 00:04:18.759
What? You want human?

00:04:19.551 --> 00:04:21.053
What's this spice for?

00:04:21.136 --> 00:04:22.387
That's powdered swamp root.

00:04:22.471 --> 00:04:24.598
Makes you irresistible
to the opposite sex.

00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:27.184
Oh, that's ridiculous.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.602
I'll take two pounds.

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.316
Hey, buddy.

00:04:34.399 --> 00:04:35.943
I'm looking for fresh slug.

00:04:36.026 --> 00:04:37.903
- Yellow or purple?
- Whatever.

00:04:37.986 --> 00:04:40.572
The purple one
causes terrible nightmarish diarrhea.

00:04:40.656 --> 00:04:42.699
Yeah, yeah, either one's fine.

00:04:42.783 --> 00:04:44.785
Hey, have you seen Fry?

00:04:45.536 --> 00:04:46.745
Now that you mention it,

00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:49.373
I do have trouble
breathing underwater sometimes.

00:04:49.456 --> 00:04:50.541
I'll take the gills.

00:04:50.624 --> 00:04:52.042
Yes, gills.

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:55.003
Then, uh, you don't need
lungs anymore, is right?

00:04:55.087 --> 00:04:56.421
Can't imagine why I would.

00:04:56.505 --> 00:04:57.714
Lie down on table.

00:04:57.798 --> 00:04:59.925
I take lungs now, gills come next week.

00:05:03.971 --> 00:05:05.347
Nurse!

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.807
Let's do it.

00:05:07.975 --> 00:05:10.102
You may feel small pain.

00:05:10.185 --> 00:05:11.854
Hyah!

00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:17.943
Thank you.

00:05:19.278 --> 00:05:20.737
What the hell were you doing?

00:05:20.821 --> 00:05:23.031
I warned you to stay away from those guys.

00:05:23.115 --> 00:05:25.701
I'm capable of making
my own decisions, Leela.

00:05:25.784 --> 00:05:28.620
Did you ever stop to think
I might be happier with gills?

00:05:28.704 --> 00:05:30.289
Good news, everyone.

00:05:30.372 --> 00:05:32.082
Uh-oh, I don't like the sound of that.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.127
You'll be making a delivery
to the planet Trisol.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.253
Here it comes.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:41.133
A mysterious world in the darkest depths
of the forbidden zone.

00:05:41.216 --> 00:05:42.759
Thank you, and good night.

00:05:42.843 --> 00:05:46.638
Uh, Professor, are we even
allowed in the forbidden zone?

00:05:46.722 --> 00:05:49.266
Why, of course. It's just a name.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:52.477
Like the Death Zone
or the Zone of No Return.

00:05:52.561 --> 00:05:56.231
All the zones have names like that
in the Galaxy of Terror.

00:05:56.315 --> 00:05:58.400
- Uh, Professor...
- Off you go.

00:05:58.483 --> 00:05:59.610
Pleasant trip.

00:06:04.072 --> 00:06:05.199
Hey, Bender

00:06:05.282 --> 00:06:07.784
- How's dinner coming?
- Almost ready.

00:06:14.541 --> 00:06:17.461
Ah, now for a dash of salt.

00:06:20.923 --> 00:06:22.883
Uh-oh.

00:06:26.678 --> 00:06:30.557
Listen, this is Bender's first meal
and he's a little sensitive.

00:06:30.641 --> 00:06:32.226
So let's be supportive, okay?

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:33.769
- Right.
- Yeah, okay.

00:06:35.062 --> 00:06:36.438
Oh, dear God!

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:41.318
Ugh. That's the saltiest thing
I've ever tasted.

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:43.529
And I once ate a big heaping bowl of salt.

00:06:46.031 --> 00:06:47.908
Bender, is this salt water?

00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:50.577
That's salt with water in it,
if that's what you mean.

00:06:50.661 --> 00:06:52.663
My vision's fading.

00:06:52.746 --> 00:06:53.914
I think I'm gonna die.

00:06:53.997 --> 00:06:56.375
There was nothing wrong with that food.

00:06:56.458 --> 00:07:00.045
The salt level was 10% less
than a lethal dose.

00:07:00.128 --> 00:07:02.297
Uh-oh, I shouldn't have had seconds.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.432
Okay, Fry, here's the package to deliver.

00:07:12.516 --> 00:07:14.685
And for once in your life, be careful.

00:07:14.768 --> 00:07:17.020
This is my first visit
to the Galaxy of Terror

00:07:17.104 --> 00:07:19.565
and I'd like it to be a pleasant one.

00:07:19.857 --> 00:07:20.858
Ow!

00:07:20.941 --> 00:07:23.193
Don't touch anything or talk to anyone.

00:07:23.277 --> 00:07:26.071
Just go to the palace,
drop it off and come right back.

00:07:26.154 --> 00:07:27.948
Geez, will you lay off?

00:07:28.031 --> 00:07:30.284
I was delivering things
before you were born.

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:32.202
I think I know what I'm doing.

00:07:41.253 --> 00:07:44.798
Oh, stupid slug.

00:07:44.882 --> 00:07:46.633
I've never been so thirsty.

00:07:47.301 --> 00:07:49.553
Oh, come on, go down already.

00:08:12.826 --> 00:08:14.745
Hello? Anybody home?

00:08:32.721 --> 00:08:34.473
Ah...

00:08:34.556 --> 00:08:36.475
The royal bottle is empty!

00:08:36.558 --> 00:08:38.977
You drank our emperor!

00:08:39.061 --> 00:08:40.771
No, it wasn't me.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:50.197
You drank our emperor!
You assassinated him!

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.742
I didn't mean to.
He just looked so cool and refreshing.

00:08:53.825 --> 00:08:55.244
I'm sure he was.

00:08:55.327 --> 00:08:58.497
But now he's gone,
and your fate is sealed.

00:09:00.082 --> 00:09:03.001
All hail the new emperor!

00:09:03.544 --> 00:09:06.046
Hail! Hail! Hail!

00:09:08.841 --> 00:09:12.511
So after I specifically
asked you not to touch anything,

00:09:12.594 --> 00:09:14.805
you drank a bottle of strange blue liquid.

00:09:14.888 --> 00:09:16.849
It could have been poisonous acid.

00:09:16.932 --> 00:09:20.018
It could have been, but chances were
equally good it was an emperor.

00:09:20.102 --> 00:09:21.520
Excuse me, Your Majesty.

00:09:21.603 --> 00:09:23.105
I am Murg, the high priest.

00:09:23.188 --> 00:09:24.356
If I might interject?

00:09:24.439 --> 00:09:25.440
You might.

00:09:25.524 --> 00:09:29.903
I humbly advise that, as your first act,
you choose a capable prime minister.

00:09:29.987 --> 00:09:32.656
I suggest Gorgak, the previous appointee.

00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:36.368
I will be a forceful
and effective administrator.

00:09:36.451 --> 00:09:39.746
You know, Fry, I've often thought
about becoming a prime minister.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:41.248
I gotta go with Bender.

00:09:41.331 --> 00:09:43.292
Yes! In your face, Gorgak!

00:09:43.375 --> 00:09:44.376
That's it, Fry.

00:09:44.459 --> 00:09:46.753
As your captain,
I order you back to the ship.

00:09:46.837 --> 00:09:48.672
You are in way over your head.

00:09:48.755 --> 00:09:50.591
Gee, you think so, Captain?

00:09:50.674 --> 00:09:52.968
I'd better check with my prime minister.

00:09:53.051 --> 00:09:54.845
Stay the course, pal.

00:09:54.928 --> 00:09:57.848
Your Highness, a package came for you.

00:09:59.016 --> 00:10:00.350
Hey, thanks.

00:10:02.769 --> 00:10:05.189
Wow, this got here just in time.

00:10:08.317 --> 00:10:10.402
This is Your Majesty's harem.

00:10:10.485 --> 00:10:13.906
You may choose any of these maidens
to be your royal consort.

00:10:13.989 --> 00:10:16.450
Uh... Uh, uh, uh... How about that one?

00:10:16.533 --> 00:10:20.329
Oh! I didn't realize Your Majesty
was into that sort of thing.

00:10:20.412 --> 00:10:23.582
On second thought, uh, I'll take that one.

00:10:23.665 --> 00:10:26.293
Hey, whatever you say.
I'm not here to pass judgment.

00:10:26.376 --> 00:10:30.464
Does anyone else think it's odd
that a shiftless, 25-year-old delivery boy

00:10:30.547 --> 00:10:32.883
could drop out of the sky,
kill the emperor

00:10:32.966 --> 00:10:34.801
and be rewarded instead of punished?

00:10:34.885 --> 00:10:36.762
You don't have to beat
around the bush, Leela.

00:10:36.845 --> 00:10:38.680
We all know who you're talking about.

00:10:39.556 --> 00:10:40.641
Me, right?

00:10:40.724 --> 00:10:43.018
Uh, I don't think
there's anything to worry about.

00:10:43.101 --> 00:10:45.062
These people seem really mild-mannered.

00:10:45.145 --> 00:10:48.815
They are mild.
In fact, you're soaking in one right now.

00:10:50.609 --> 00:10:55.239
You touched me in ways
I've never been touched before.

00:10:55.322 --> 00:10:57.199
Ah, there you are, Your Majesty.

00:10:57.282 --> 00:11:00.786
It's time to begin preparing
for tomorrow's coronation ceremony.

00:11:00.869 --> 00:11:04.581
A fancy dress gala?
I'll wear my formal shell.

00:11:04.665 --> 00:11:07.835
Fry will be enthroned tomorrow
at the setting of the three suns,

00:11:07.918 --> 00:11:10.796
when we Trisolians
enter our nocturnal phase.

00:11:10.879 --> 00:11:13.382
There won't be a lot
of long-winded speeches, will there?

00:11:13.465 --> 00:11:14.800
Only one.

00:11:14.883 --> 00:11:19.638
The absolutely flawless recitation
from memory of the royal oath...

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:21.139
by you.

00:11:21.223 --> 00:11:22.599
Will there be cake?

00:11:25.352 --> 00:11:27.813
- Yeah, I know.
- Hi!

00:11:29.106 --> 00:11:31.066
- There you go.
- Mmm!

00:11:37.865 --> 00:11:41.618
And now, get ready to laugh
till your sides leak

00:11:41.702 --> 00:11:46.123
with our planet's foremost
political satirist, Florp.

00:11:50.043 --> 00:11:53.797
So what is the deal with people
from under the orange sun?

00:11:53.881 --> 00:11:56.550
They're all...

00:11:59.386 --> 00:12:02.514
But us guys from under
the red sun, we're like...

00:12:06.602 --> 00:12:08.312
Right? Am I right?

00:12:08.395 --> 00:12:10.522
Oh, yeah, he's right.

00:12:11.481 --> 00:12:13.317
Fry, I have to talk to you.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.902
You're in terrible danger.

00:12:15.569 --> 00:12:17.196
You see emperor Plon here?

00:12:17.279 --> 00:12:20.282
He met his end
when he was drunk by Emperor Strug.

00:12:20.365 --> 00:12:22.409
And before he could even wipe his mouth,

00:12:22.492 --> 00:12:24.161
Strug was drunk by Shwab.

00:12:24.244 --> 00:12:26.246
- So?
- Look at all these guys.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:29.291
Do you have any idea what
the average length of their reigns was?

00:12:29.374 --> 00:12:31.376
Uh... 80,000 years?

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.253
No, one week.

00:12:33.337 --> 00:12:37.549
Damn. I knew you wouldn't have asked
unless it was really high or really low.

00:12:37.633 --> 00:12:41.345
Every emperor ascended to power
by assassinating the previous one.

00:12:41.428 --> 00:12:43.138
And guess who's next?

00:12:46.016 --> 00:12:48.852
Well, at least my assassin
will get what's coming to him.

00:12:48.936 --> 00:12:51.355
You're in tremendous danger, you idiot!

00:12:51.438 --> 00:12:54.233
Half these emperors
were drunk at their own coronation.

00:12:54.316 --> 00:12:57.236
Hey, I plan on having
a few brewskis myself.

00:12:57.319 --> 00:12:59.321
No, they were assassinated.

00:12:59.404 --> 00:13:01.907
In fact, the law says
you'll be killed on the spot

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.284
if you fail to recite
the oath from memory.

00:13:04.868 --> 00:13:06.787
Yeah, I was gonna
thumb through that later.

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:09.331
That is completely reckless.

00:13:09.414 --> 00:13:11.083
Don't you ever think ahead?

00:13:11.166 --> 00:13:12.167
Hell, no.

00:13:12.251 --> 00:13:15.003
If I stopped to think ahead,
I wouldn't be emperor,

00:13:15.087 --> 00:13:17.548
and I wouldn't even be here
in the year 3000.

00:13:17.631 --> 00:13:20.926
It's just like the story
of the grasshopper and the octopus.

00:13:21.009 --> 00:13:24.888
All year long, the grasshopper
kept burying acorns for winter

00:13:24.972 --> 00:13:28.642
while the octopus mooched off
his girlfriend and watched TV.

00:13:28.725 --> 00:13:31.520
But then the winter came
and the grasshopper died,

00:13:31.603 --> 00:13:35.482
and the octopus ate all his acorns
and also, he got a race car.

00:13:35.566 --> 00:13:37.484
Is any of this getting through to you?

00:13:37.568 --> 00:13:40.237
Ugh. I give up.
You're gonna get yourself killed,

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:42.447
and this time,
I won't be able to save you.

00:13:42.531 --> 00:13:43.740
Who asked you to?

00:13:43.824 --> 00:13:46.535
I told you a hundred times
to stop treating me like a baby.

00:13:46.618 --> 00:13:50.497
Now go. Go gather your nuts,
you nagging grasshopper.

00:13:50.581 --> 00:13:53.542
That's it! I'm never helping you again.

00:13:53.625 --> 00:13:56.628
If anyone except you needs me,
I'll be in the ship.

00:13:56.712 --> 00:13:58.213
I'll be fine.

00:13:58.297 --> 00:14:00.340
It's not like anyone's gonna drink me.

00:14:03.302 --> 00:14:04.469
Quit it.

00:14:09.183 --> 00:14:10.434
People of Trisol,

00:14:10.517 --> 00:14:13.854
it is my honor to present
your new emperor.

00:14:19.151 --> 00:14:21.403
What up?

00:14:24.072 --> 00:14:25.490
Stick to the oath.

00:14:25.574 --> 00:14:26.700
Right.

00:14:26.783 --> 00:14:30.787
I, Fry, who drank Bont the Viscous,

00:14:30.871 --> 00:14:32.789
who drank Ungo the Moist,

00:14:32.873 --> 00:14:35.250
who guzzled Zorn the Stagnant,

00:14:35.918 --> 00:14:37.711
who slurped Hudj the Dewy,

00:14:37.794 --> 00:14:41.798
who enjoyed a soup composed
principally of Throm the Chunky,

00:14:41.882 --> 00:14:45.135
do solemnly swear
to rule with honor and...

00:14:46.303 --> 00:14:47.346
insanity...

00:14:47.429 --> 00:14:49.097
uh, integrity.

00:14:49.181 --> 00:14:51.099
Congratulations, Your Highness.

00:14:52.142 --> 00:14:55.687
I now present you
with your royal unisex robe.

00:14:55.771 --> 00:14:58.690
Long live Fry the Solid!

00:15:03.445 --> 00:15:05.447
Hey, look, the suns are setting.

00:15:05.531 --> 00:15:08.033
I can finally switch to hard liquor.

00:15:10.494 --> 00:15:11.495
Ah.

00:15:21.296 --> 00:15:23.173
Check out the glowing freaks.

00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:24.967
It's beautiful.

00:15:25.509 --> 00:15:26.760
Hey, what's that?

00:15:30.514 --> 00:15:31.849
The emperor Bont!

00:15:32.516 --> 00:15:34.226
He's still alive!

00:15:34.309 --> 00:15:36.103
Of course I'm alive.

00:15:36.186 --> 00:15:38.480
Now cut this creep open and drain me out.

00:15:40.816 --> 00:15:42.317
My tummy hurts.

00:15:48.031 --> 00:15:50.576
They're over here.
They're running up the stairs.

00:15:50.659 --> 00:15:52.119
Shut up, you.

00:15:58.250 --> 00:15:59.251
Let us in!

00:15:59.334 --> 00:16:01.920
Fry must die so that bont may live.

00:16:02.004 --> 00:16:03.797
What am I gonna do?

00:16:03.881 --> 00:16:07.134
We've gotta get the emperor
out of your body before they kill you.

00:16:07.217 --> 00:16:08.468
Relax, Fry.

00:16:08.552 --> 00:16:11.471
I'll simply spin you
in a high-speed centrifuge,

00:16:11.555 --> 00:16:14.474
separating out
the denser fluid of His Highness.

00:16:14.558 --> 00:16:15.934
But won't that crush my bones?

00:16:16.018 --> 00:16:18.103
Oh, right, right, with the bones.

00:16:18.187 --> 00:16:20.689
I always forget about the bones.

00:16:20.772 --> 00:16:22.691
Hey, why don't you just sweat him out?

00:16:22.774 --> 00:16:23.775
Forget it.

00:16:23.859 --> 00:16:27.237
As emperor, I refuse to be dripped out
through somebody's armpit.

00:16:27.321 --> 00:16:30.657
I could vomit or urinate.
Would you feel better about that?

00:16:30.741 --> 00:16:33.577
Slightly. But my favorite so far
is the bone crushing.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:34.870
What about crying?

00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:37.289
That's a great idea. Crying.

00:16:37.372 --> 00:16:38.999
Fine. That or the bone one.

00:16:42.419 --> 00:16:45.255
Keep it up, men.
The veneer is starting to peel.

00:16:46.423 --> 00:16:48.050
Oh, dear.

00:16:50.135 --> 00:16:53.263
It's no use.
I wanna cry, but I'm just too macho.

00:16:53.347 --> 00:16:55.224
I'll make you cry, buddy.

00:16:55.307 --> 00:16:58.393
You're a pimple on society's ass

00:16:58.477 --> 00:17:00.479
and you'll never amount to anything.

00:17:00.562 --> 00:17:03.315
What do you mean?
I was emperor of a whole planet.

00:17:03.398 --> 00:17:04.441
Good point.

00:17:04.525 --> 00:17:06.860
But here's a disturbing reminder,

00:17:06.944 --> 00:17:11.949
everyone you knew or loved
in the 20th century is dead.

00:17:12.032 --> 00:17:14.034
- These things happen.
- Argh.

00:17:14.117 --> 00:17:16.995
Okay, Fry, grab a Kleenex for this one

00:17:17.079 --> 00:17:18.664
'cause there's no god

00:17:18.747 --> 00:17:22.918
and your idiotic human ideals
are laughable.

00:17:23.919 --> 00:17:24.920
Whew.

00:17:25.003 --> 00:17:26.964
That's a load off my mind.

00:17:27.047 --> 00:17:30.300
Man, I guess it's harder than I thought
to make someone cry.

00:17:30.384 --> 00:17:31.969
You did your best, Bender.

00:17:32.052 --> 00:17:33.512
Up yours, bimbo!

00:17:35.764 --> 00:17:37.975
Let's face it, we're in hot butter here.

00:17:38.058 --> 00:17:39.810
We should call Leela for help.

00:17:39.893 --> 00:17:40.894
Cram it, lobster.

00:17:42.145 --> 00:17:44.439
But that is a good idea. I'll go call her.

00:17:44.898 --> 00:17:46.817
Eh, she'll never help me.

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:49.319
She's still mad that I told her
never to help me.

00:17:49.403 --> 00:17:52.364
Come on, Leela's not the type
to hold a grudge.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.538
Collect call from...

00:17:59.621 --> 00:18:02.416
I'm not giving my name
to a machine!

00:18:02.499 --> 00:18:03.709
I'll accept.

00:18:04.293 --> 00:18:06.545
Fry's in trouble and he needs help.

00:18:06.628 --> 00:18:08.881
Now, I don't like you
and you don't like me...

00:18:08.964 --> 00:18:11.049
- I like you.
- You do?

00:18:11.133 --> 00:18:13.677
Ah. Look, are you gonna help or not?

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:15.888
I don't know why I should.
I mean, after what he...

00:18:15.971 --> 00:18:16.972
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:18:17.055 --> 00:18:19.099
What is it you like best about me?

00:18:20.058 --> 00:18:21.185
Is she coming?

00:18:21.268 --> 00:18:25.772
I'm not sure, but I do know
that she likes my in-your-face attitude.

00:18:34.698 --> 00:18:35.949
What the hell is that?

00:18:36.033 --> 00:18:38.160
It's the Juice-A-Matic 4000.

00:18:38.243 --> 00:18:41.246
It'll strain my juices from you
while filtering out the pulp.

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:43.832
By which I mean your shredded remains.

00:18:43.916 --> 00:18:46.877
Of course. Why didn't I think of that?

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.046
This is the saddest day of my life

00:18:49.129 --> 00:18:51.423
and I still can't cry.

00:18:53.675 --> 00:18:54.676
Wait a second.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:55.802
Here comes Leela!

00:19:05.312 --> 00:19:08.190
Oh, no. They have her totally outnumbered.

00:19:08.273 --> 00:19:09.316
I can't believe it.

00:19:09.399 --> 00:19:12.861
She's risking her life for me
after the way I treated her?

00:19:12.945 --> 00:19:15.072
Oh, I don't deserve this.

00:19:15.155 --> 00:19:16.615
I feel terrible.

00:19:16.698 --> 00:19:18.992
You do? Hmm...

00:19:19.076 --> 00:19:21.745
- Is she all right?
- Uh, I don't know.

00:19:21.828 --> 00:19:24.331
Perhaps I'll look out this window.

00:19:25.207 --> 00:19:28.544
Oh, dear God in heaven!
They're swarming all over her!

00:19:28.627 --> 00:19:30.087
No! no!

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:32.089
What are you talking about, Bender?
She's...

00:19:32.172 --> 00:19:33.757
Mm.

00:19:33.841 --> 00:19:36.260
There's strapping her to the juicer!

00:19:36.343 --> 00:19:39.680
Oh, they're putting some ice cubes
in the glass under it.

00:19:41.306 --> 00:19:43.308
This can't be happening!

00:19:43.392 --> 00:19:46.353
It can, and for all you know, it is.

00:19:48.647 --> 00:19:51.149
Oh, I'm sorry, Fry.

00:19:51.859 --> 00:19:53.360
She's dead.

00:19:59.658 --> 00:20:02.077
All Leela ever wanted to do was help me

00:20:02.619 --> 00:20:05.873
And I was too proud
and stupid to accept it.

00:20:06.582 --> 00:20:08.625
I wish I had died instead of her.

00:20:09.084 --> 00:20:10.794
What are you talking about?

00:20:12.004 --> 00:20:13.755
Leela! You're alive!

00:20:13.839 --> 00:20:15.382
Of course I'm alive.

00:20:15.465 --> 00:20:18.927
I told Fry you were dead
so he would cry out the emperor,

00:20:19.011 --> 00:20:21.388
but you had to go
and wreck it by surviving.

00:20:21.471 --> 00:20:22.973
We only got two drops.

00:20:23.056 --> 00:20:24.850
What the...

00:20:28.812 --> 00:20:30.772
It's only a matter of time now.

00:20:30.856 --> 00:20:32.566
I'll handle this.

00:20:36.278 --> 00:20:38.864
Listen, Fry,
I think I can get us out of this

00:20:38.947 --> 00:20:40.908
if you're willing to let me help you.

00:20:40.991 --> 00:20:42.326
Thanks, Leela.

00:20:42.409 --> 00:20:45.370
From now on, I'll take all the help
you're willing to give.

00:20:45.454 --> 00:20:47.497
I know you just want what's best for me.

00:20:50.459 --> 00:20:52.377
Ow! What was that for?

00:20:52.961 --> 00:20:54.129
Hey, come on!

00:20:54.213 --> 00:20:55.672
That hurt!

00:20:55.756 --> 00:20:57.883
I know.
Amy, get the bottle.

00:21:00.052 --> 00:21:02.012
Ow!

00:21:02.095 --> 00:21:03.764
Oh, now I understand.

00:21:03.847 --> 00:21:06.308
Come on. Everybody help out Fry.

00:21:06.391 --> 00:21:09.144
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:21:10.812 --> 00:21:13.273
Thanks, everybody.
I love you all.

00:21:14.441 --> 00:21:15.776
You guys are true... Oh!

00:21:15.859 --> 00:21:18.820
Cut it out, Bender. That's a tender area.

00:21:19.863 --> 00:21:20.864
How we doing, Amy?

00:21:20.948 --> 00:21:23.700
Great. We're one-tenth of the way there.

00:21:29.831 --> 00:21:32.584
Okay, it's your turn.

00:21:35.128 --> 00:21:37.756
Hey, wait a minute. Who are you?

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:39.132
I'm the emperor.

00:21:39.216 --> 00:21:41.218
Thanks for crying me out.

00:21:42.427 --> 00:21:43.554
Oh, you're welcome.

00:21:48.642 --> 00:21:50.519
Hey, save some for me!